{"availability":"available","full":"Jorricks/macos-notifications","name":"macos-notifications","description":"Create interactable notifications in the Notification Centre on any Mac using Python","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":93,"forks":4,"created":"2022-07-23T11:50:38Z","updated":"2024-10-12T08:48:14Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://jorricks.github.io/macos-notifications/","topics":["apple","mac","macos","notificationcenter","notifications"],"demo":"https://jorricks.github.io/macos-notifications/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:22.288Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:22.288Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:22.288Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T05:49:22.288Z","stars":93,"forks":4}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["mac-notification is a Python library to make it as easy as possible to create interactable notifications.","I wanted a library that did not depend on any non-python tools (so you had to go around and install that). Instead, I wanted a library where you install the pip packages, and you are done. Later I realised how hard it was to integrate correctly with PyOBJC. Also, I had a hard time finding any examples on how to easily integrate this in a non-blocking fashion with my tool. Hence, I figured I should set it up to be as user-friendly as possible and share it with the world ;)!"],"features":["🚀 Easy python interface. It's as simple as 'client.createnotification(title=\"Meeting starts now!\", subtitle=\"Team Standup\")'","💥 Ability to add action buttons with callbacks!","📝 Ability to reply to notifications!","⌚ Delayed notifications.","⏱️ Automatically time out the notification listener."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Jorricks/macos-notifications/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"580265cd20ca57e5493fccec15f68627fa5781ff1a9a6d9be3af267730efb8f7","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T05:49:22.461Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-1